                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-4">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How long does trademark opposition take in Pune?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>The complete process typically takes 2-4 years from filing to final decision. The initial opposition window is 4 months from journal publication. The applicant has 2 months for a counter statement. Evidence submission and hearings add 6-18 months. Online hearings at the Mumbai Registry have helped reduce delays.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-5">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What happens if I do not file a counter statement?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Under the Trade Marks Rules, 2017, if the applicant fails to file a counter statement within 2 months of receiving the opposition notice, the trademark application is deemed abandoned and the mark will not proceed to registration.</p></div>
